      "tier": "standard",
      "headline": "Week 7 Preview: Unbeaten Streaks Collide in Wabbits-Vitside",
      "body": "Wascawy Wabbits and Vitside Mafia have both won four straight, and the Wabbits own the series 12-4. Plus a streak that should snap and the two NFL games to keep on.",
      "franchiseIds": [],
      "link": "/theleague/news/sf_2026_matchup_preview_w07",
      "linkLabel": "Read matchup preview",
      "league": "theleague",
      "authorId": "claude",
      "content": [
        "<p>Game of the Week: Wascawy Wabbits and Vitside Mafia have both won four straight, and something has to give. The Wabbits lead the series 12-4 and won the only playoff meeting, but Josh Allen (28.6) has Vitside projected 148.1 to 141.1. I'm taking Vitside. Watch it on <a href=\"/theleague/live-scoring\">the live scoreboard</a>.</p>",
        "<p>Midwestside Connection have won all 8 meetings with Cowboy Up, and this is the week it ends. Joe Burrow (24.2) has Cowboy Up projected 112.9 to 96.8. Pacific Pigskins have won 8 straight, and Jared Goff (26.8) makes it 9 against Fire Ready Aim, 133.0 to 105.7.</p>",
        "<p>Maverick is 0-9, but this series with Gridiron Geeks is dead even at 7-7. Patrick Mahomes (24.0) keeps it closer than 113.1 to 128.2 looks. Geeks, set <a href=\"/theleague/lineup\">your lineup</a> before kickoff anyway.</p>",
        "<p>Broadcast guide: Cincinnati is the must-watch, with Joe Burrow, Ja'Marr Chase, Tee Higgins and Chase Brown spread across four teams. Detroit is next, with Jared Goff, Jahmyr Gibbs, Sam LaPorta and Amon-Ra St. Brown. Plan your multiview on <a href=\"/theleague/sunday-ticket\">the Sunday Ticket board</a>, then follow <a href=\"/theleague/live-scoring\">the scoreboard</a>.</p>"
      ],
